From 1248c08818d8ee6ad72056430e8212be34818ab8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z <z@z.ai>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:14:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Specials and mods are back!

The loadout UI could no longer add weapon specials or mods: the item
detail panel only rendered a Special/Mod row when one was already
equipped, so empty slots were invisible and unclickable on any fresh
build. Part rows now always render, with a click-to-choose empty state.

Also fixes repeater part slots: the Mod row was hard-wired to
weaponPart2, so clicking it opened the grip picker and would overwrite
the equipped grip. Part rows now carry their slot key directly
(chamber=p1, grip=p2, mod=p3 for repeaters; special=p1, mod=p2 for
everything else).

Bonus: equipped parts now show their interpolated ability text in the
weapon detail card (Special - <name>: ...), the part picker shows the
same text so players can compare before equipping, and the Part type
was corrected to match data.json (part_effect/values instead of the
nonexistent perks/unique_effects/description on most entries).

Verified: 35/35 bun tests (roundtrips, bucket routing, v7->v9 upgrade
keeps parts, legacy build regression, data completeness), tsc clean,
and a full browser click-through of sword and repeater builds with
share-link roundtrips.
